<title>CANADA: Canada new housing price index falls in December.</title>
<headline>Canada new housing price index falls in December.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's new housing price index fell 0.9 percent in December to 131.9 (base 1986) from December 1995, Statistics Canada said on Monday.</p>
<p>    Index			  Dec     yr pct  month pct</p>
<p> Total			    131.9     -0.9	+0.1</p>
<p> House only		     121.7     -1.1	+0.1</p>
<p> Land only			165.4     -0.4	+0.1</p>
<p>The index measures changes of contractors' selling prices of new residential houses.</p>
<p>A Reuter survey of economists had forecast a 0.8 percent drop in the annual index.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
</text>
